            "commit": "9683dc30298f30e6e2ea11c732b8a0de0ac9fcab",
            "subject": "LU-20730 llapi: remove the scan record interface"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Hiroshi Nishida",
          "email": "hnishida@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-13 05:49:19.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Hiroshi Nishida",
          "email": "hnishida@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-20 21:50:40.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-20637 lfs: grow -printf over a target as a walk does",
        "message": "LU-20637 lfs: grow -printf over a target as a walk does\n\nlfs find --device -printf keeps its output in pieces until each\npathname is known.  The pieces were built in a fixed 1024-byte\nbuffer and kept in a 2048-byte blob, so a format with %LO for a wide\nor overstriped file lost the rest of its line, newline included, and\nthe next match ran on.  A walk grows its buffer up to\nFORMATTED_BUF_MAX.  Grow the target scan's buffers the same way,\nand redo a %p that fills the space left, as a walk does.\n\nconf-sanity 307 compares a walk and a target scan over an\noverstriped file, and the padding of a %p wider than PATH_MAX.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=307\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I7d52824b19c5954ce4d4c9b53cb0ebe3ba277fd6\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
